        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8226c8fa-8c50-5b96-bdf1-f9377bcfbfd6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Władysław Grydziuszko\n- Products: Douglas SBD Dauntless, Curtiss SB2C Helldiver\n- Ships: Tama Maru No. 2, USS Lexington, USS Yorktown\n- Events: Invasion of Lae-Salamaua, World War II\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n\nFacts:\n- Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless, an American naval scout plane and dive bomber, from 1940 through 1944 during World War II.\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown damaged the Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2 off Lae, New Guinea.\n- The Curtiss SB2C Helldiver replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in United States Navy service.\n- Sergeant Władysław Grydziuszko (1910–1946) served as a soldier in the Polish Army during World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c4e87367-704d-5af2-b57a-f5f221cf07a7",
        "text": "Page: Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2. Sentence: On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, \"Tama Maru No. 2\" was damaged by Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the United States Navy aircraft carriers USS \"Lexington\" and USS \"Yorktown\" off Lae, New Guinea.\nPage: Douglas SBD Dauntless. Sentence: The Douglas SBD Dauntless was a World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber that was manufactured by Douglas Aircraft from 1940 through 1944.\nPage: Curtiss SB2C Helldiver. Sentence: It replaced the Douglas SBD Dauntless in US Navy service.\nPage: Władysław Grydziuszko. Sentence: Sergeant Władysław Grydziuszko (1910–1946) was a soldier in the Polish Army during World War II.",
